I have a digital personal workstation 500au (aka miata).
I have downloaded the iso images of Red Hat 7.2 alpha and burn them onto
CDs but :
If I want to boot from the CD, I put CD1 in my driver and at the SRM
prompt type
>>> boot DKA0 -flags 0
(DKA0 is my CD-rom driver). It start reading the disk and then after the
message
>>> jumping to bootstrap code
It crashes and just HALT my CPU. It does not want to boot from the CD.
Then I boot Tru64Unix, mount the CD1 to create a bootable floppy.
I type
# dd if=generic.img of=/dev/fd0c bs=72k
and the same for the RAM disk
After that, I try to boot from the Floppy (at SRM) :
>>> boot DVA0 -flags 0
And it says that
>>> Block 0 of DVA0 is not a valid boot block
So it seems that the floppy is not bootable.
Is Red Hat 7.2 compatible for Miata ?
If yes, I don't know what else to do.

Romain




