2.5.74 causes 2 problems:
        a) keyboard caps-/num-/scrolllock or led problem
        b) bttv compile problem

a) in drivers/input/keyboard/atkbd.c function atkbd_event() i had to
comment the 2 atkbd_command() calls. otherwise the screen freezes if
caps-, num- or scrolllock are pressed. if the calls are commented then
the led's dont work, but the funktionality is fine.

it seems that the problem occurs in atkbd_command() within
these commends:
===
        if (command & 0xff)
                if (atkbd_sendbyte(atkbd, command & 0xff))
                        return (atkbd->cmdcnt = 0) - 1;
===
a printk before that lines appears on the screen.
printk's after that lines dont appear on the screen
if you press one of the 3 buttons...

b) in drivers/media/video/bttv-risc.c i had to #include <asm/io.h>.
otherwise writel and readl funktions are missing when linking the
kernel (on alpha they are defined in that header file -- dont know
about other architectures...)

happy coding, niki



