Hi there,

bit quiet in here lately...

Am I the only one or has anyone else notice the bewildering amount of choice
that is becoming available in systems cpus etc..

First of all lets start with the humble pc

why not have a AMD duron 1.2ghz - £20 + a motherboard for £40 memory etc
that won't cost much - that'll do nicely.

Maybe not how about something more exotic

Athlon MP

no

P4 then - hyperthreading, 800mhz bus? NO P5 will be along shortly no to
bland

Xeon? - 512, 1mb cache No? Xeon MP - Too expensive?

64bit then - Opteron? which flavour 140, 244, 842? No maybe 246?

Well there's always AMD64? Not available yet.

Itanium then - Itanium II? Madison? - 1.3ghz? or 1.5ghz? 1.5, 3, 6 mb cache?

Confused? Well maybe we'll turn to OS?

Windows? 32bit or 64bit? XP 64 - bit - not available, WIndows 2003 server
x86 or 64-bit Itanium, no want it for opteron? no you'll have to have 32bit
for that sir?

Well there's always Linux  - 64 bit Suse - how much? Debian then that's
free - sorry not availbale - yet, RH -

Oh well there's always HP-UX - only for itanium from HP.

VMS !

____________________________________________________________

Oh well how much simpler things were back in the day of the Alpha, 1 64bit
cpu whether you wanted a 1 processor Windows PC/Workstation or a >64
processor supercomputer running UNIX.

Sigh


