On Mon, 7 Jul 2003, Peter Watkinson wrote:

>64bit then - Opteron? which flavour 140, 244, 842? No maybe 246?
>
>Well there's always AMD64? Not available yet.

AMD64 is the name of the actual architecture - formerly known as 
"x86_64".  "Opteron" is the name of AMD's initial public 
implementation of the AMD64 architecture for enterprise usage 
(previously codenamed Sledgehammer).  "Athlon 64" is AMD's 
current public marketing name for the consumer version of the 
AMD64 technology which is allegedly to be released to the public 
in the fall sometime - previously codenamed "Clawhammer".

Both the Opteron, and the Athlon 64 chips are AMD64 architecture.  
So, while "Athlon 64" isn't available yet, AMD64 architecture is 
available right now - the Opteron.


>Itanium then - Itanium II? Madison? - 1.3ghz? or 1.5ghz? 1.5, 3, 6 mb cache?

Um... why?  Is your house cold or something?  ;o)  I'd wait a bit
longer until they get those BTU numbers up a bit and you can turn
your furnace off completely.  ;o)




