On Wed, 9 Jul 2003, Romain Guerout wrote:

>I have a miata running Red Hat 7.2 with a Powerstorm 4DxxT graphic card.
>It seems that this card is not supported by
>XFree86 4.3.0 (which I have).
>Does anyone know a X server (even commercial) which support this card ?
>Does anyone know if another distribution of Linux (Suse, Debian, ...)
>can support this card ?

It isn't a Red Hat constraint.  That video card is just 
completely unsupported by XFree86.  There arent' any proprietary 
drivers available for it either to the best of my knowledge.

Before anyone asks - it will never be supported by XFree86 
either, as it is ancient hardware, and the company who made it 
no longer exists (to my knowledge) and no docs are available.

The only way to use it in Linux, is to take it out and use it as 
a windowstick or something, and put in a supported card.  ;o)


-- 
