In fact, I have discover something :
Mt miata has 2 graphic cards (I didn't even knew about it)
- a Powerstrom 4D60T with 32Mb which is the primary device and is used
by Tru64Unix
- and a Cirrus Logic GD5430 which is not used I think
Because the Powerstorm is not supported by XFree86, I think I can use
the Cirrus card for Linux.
The problem is that if I run "startx" with the Cirrus, I see in the log
file that this card has only 512 kb of RAM.
Because this card is not used, I think that there is no memory
"attached" to it.
What should I do so that the Cirrus card use more RAM memory ?

