On Wed, Jul 09, 2003 at 01:50:15PM +0200, Romain Guerout wrote:
>
> In fact, I have discover something :
> My miata has 2 graphic cards (I didn't even knew about it)
> - a Powerstrom 4D60T with 32Mb which is the primary device and is used
> by Tru64Unix
> - and a Cirrus Logic GD5430 which is not used I think

The 4D60T is actually two cards, and takes 2 PCI slots.

The Cirrus Logic chip is there to provide ONLY text mode console support,
and has only a small amount of memory (512KB?), which cannot be expanded,
AFAIK. You could check the card that the Cirrus is on, see if there are
any additional sockets for memory chips, but I think there will not be.

> Because the Powerstorm is not supported by XFree86, I think I can use
> the Cirrus card for Linux.

Well, if only 512KB is available, 800x600 at depth 8 uses nearly all
of it. Then there's the problem that the Cirrus driver, AFAIK, has
never been fully debugged on Alpha, so there may be "issues".

Really, the best idea is to find a replacement card, if you are
intending to run XFree86 under Linux. If you wish to keep the 4D60T
for use under Tru64, then you have a difficult situation... :-\

Good luck.

