XFree86 4.x doesn't support all the S3 cards that 3.3.6 supports 
(not yet, anyways).  There's a lot of S3 cards with oddball 
RAMDACs that XFree86 4.x hasn't yet been equipped to handle; I'm 
betting yours is one of them.

FWIW, I'm in the same tight spot.

> May be, anybody can tell me what version of XFree86 is usable
> or send me correct XF86config file for same hardware
> (may be I have bad hands :-)

Probably a good idea to stick with 3.3.6 or get a different card.  
I would recommend a Radeon 7200/7500 PCI.  I'd get one myself 
but can't afford it at the moment...

-- 
