It turns out that 4.3.0 added support for:

	S3 964
	S3 968
	S3 Trio64
	S3 Trio64V+

to the existing support for S3 ViRGE.

I've just done a bit of testing on an SX164 and found:

1. the (plain) Trio64 seems to work fine in 8bit and 16bit, though
   with a few screen transients that disappear very quickly, and
   forced to use SW cursor.

2. the Trio64V+, maybe aka AuroraV+, does NOT work well at all; lots
   of transients as well as long lasting glitches, bad video modes,
   and doesn't shutdown from X back to text mode cleanly at all.

3. the (plain) S3ViRGE (86c325) also seems to work quite well, with
   less problems than the (plain) Trio64.

> > May be, anybody can tell me what version of XFree86 is usable
> > or send me correct XF86config file for same hardware
> > (may be I have bad hands :-)
> 
> Probably a good idea to stick with 3.3.6 or get a different card.  
> I would recommend a Radeon 7200/7500 PCI.  I'd get one myself 
> but can't afford it at the moment...

Oh, yes, Radeon 7500 is one of my favorite cards, and works well
in both 2D and 3D. 4.3.0 puportedly will work in 2D on the Radeon
9x00 series cards, but I think the PCI versions are very rare...

Good luck.

