On Friday 11 July 2003 04:38 pm, Jay Estabrook wrote:
> 2. the Trio64V+, maybe aka AuroraV+, does NOT work well at
> all; lots of transients as well as long lasting glitches, bad
> video modes, and doesn't shutdown from X back to text mode
> cleanly at all.

Yup, this is the exact card I have, and the exact same problems.  
Basically horizontal shearing/snow splatters across the display 
frequently, and there's pretty much no way to get from X back to 
a text console without locking up the machine.  It's behaved 
like this in every XFree86 version since 4.2.0, including 
4.3.0.1 (and maybe before 4.2.0).

> > Probably a good idea to stick with 3.3.6 or get a different
> > card. I would recommend a Radeon 7200/7500 PCI.  I'd get one
> > myself but can't afford it at the moment...
>
> Oh, yes, Radeon 7500 is one of my favorite cards, and works
> well in both 2D and 3D. 4.3.0 puportedly will work in 2D on
> the Radeon 9x00 series cards, but I think the PCI versions are
> very rare...

Well, the PCI versions (both 7x00 and 9x00) are in steady supply 
on eBay, though not always cheaply.  There are some accounts of 
the 9x00 cards not working in all SRM consoles, though.  
Basically it seems as if the SRM's x86 emulation doesn't always 
work well enough to support the VGA option ROM on those cards.  
More recent boards like the UP2000 have a better shot at that 
than, say, my somewhat decrepit PC164LX. ;)

Of course, it might be possible to boot the box via a serial 
terminal, then get X to start with the Int10 option.  That's 
dreadfully unwieldly, though, and I have not the money to buy a 
9100 and test such an idea.

-- 
