On Wednesday 16 July 2003 03:00 am, Chupakhin Alexey wrote:
> I'm with 4.3.0 and video is working fine, but some new
> troubles are here:
> 1. My scroller on intellimouse is not work. I tried "ImPS"
> protocol for it (like in 3.3.6) but without results. Then I
> tried ALL supported protocols and cant make it working. May
> be, is it bug in 4.3.0?

Well, you have to do more than just specify mouse protocol to get 
scroll wheel action going.  The critical thing is 
ZAxisMapping--the up and down motion of the scroll wheel appears 
to XFree86 to be merely a fourth and fifth mouse button in 
action.  So you have to tell XFree86 that the fourth and fifth 
mouse buttons drive the "Z" (scrolling) axis.

Here's my mouse config section.  It's for a Logitech TrackMan 
Marble+ (PS/2 optical trackball with scroll wheel), but it 
should work for most other scrolling mice as well:

Section "InputDevice"
        Identifier      "Mouse0"
        Driver          "mouse"
        Option          "Protocol"      "IMPS/2"
        # Set "Device" to your mouse device file.
        Option          "Device"        "/dev/psaux"
        Option          "ZAxisMapping"  "4 5"
EndSection


> 2. System console fonts (cyrillic) just broken.

I've never gotten cyrillic fonts to install, and I've been 
building XFree86 from source since the first 4.x release.  I 
don't know why it doesn't install these fonts.  Never really 
cared much either (I typically just use Type1 and TrueType 
fonts).

-- 
Kelledin
