   Hello everyone,

   A few hours ago I finished building and installing a new xfree86-4.3 (wanted
to get support for my new Radeon 7500 on miata). After restling with
configuration for a while, I got Xserver up and running. Even with kde. However
there's a strange problem - at the end of xinitrc there are lines

exec /usr/kde/bin/startkde &
#
exec xterm -geometry 80x66+0+0 -name login

  The last one came there by default and without it X refused to startup 
(it starts and then exits with no errors). So now I have this xterm running 
and if I kill it, then X will terminate. 'ps -ef' shows 

root     21482 21477  0 03:08 tty1     00:00:00 xterm -geometry 80x66+0+0 -name
root     21486 21482  0 03:08 tty1     00:00:00 /bin/sh /usr/kde/bin/startkde

  startkde has its parent process as this xterm. Did anyone has this problem
with 4.3? How can I make it work without this default xterm?

  Thank you,


                                      Arc C.
                                      achapkis@dls.net



