On Thu, 17 Jul 2003, Arkadiy Chapkis - Arc wrote:

>  I apologize for the previous email - hit the wrong key.
>Have a question though - I just finished compiling new KDE (couple weeks
>project) on my multia (PWS500a) with Matrox card. Somehow I thought that
>upgrading the card to ATI Radeon 7500 (as it was discussed here) will give me a
>better graphic perfomance. So I did that yesterday, and it doesn't seem to be
>any faster in re-drawing stuff in XFree. Then I thought I'd better upgrade
>XFree86 from 4.1 (RH updates) to 4.3 (RawHide found on rpmfind.net). However in
>a process of doing so it seems I need to update glibc as well. The RawHide once
>cause some of the commands (rpm is one of them) to segfault.
>
>  Is there any better was to get XFree86-4.3 with support for Radeon? Is it
>worth the effort?

The current unmodified rawhide XFree86 4.3.0 src.rpm requires 
rawhide gcc/glibc to compile and has only been built on 
x86/AMD64/ia64/ppc/ppc64/s390/s390x.  It enables thread local 
storage (TLS) and libGL optimizations.

By disabling both, it should build on RHL 9 and RHL 8.0 without 
much work.  (I build it locally on RHL 8.0)

May or may not require more effort for Alpha, haven't tried on 
Alpha.


-- 
