List-Archive: <https://www.redhat.com/mailman/private/axp-list/>

If you remove the '&' from the end of the startkde line, things should work
as expected.
X requires that there be a foreground task running (and using X).  When you
kill the foreground task X exits.  The foreground task typically is your
window manager, or your desktop environment, however it can be a web
browser, script (useful for building kiosks), xterm, or even FreeCell.

Hope this helps...

