to the list:

I have been going over the archives here and other lists to see 
what kinds of memory might work on my PWS 500a.  I am waiting 
for the right deal on an XP1000, so I wanted to get memory that 
would work on that, if/when I got it.

What kind of memory? for the Miata, some say PC66, some say 
PC100; some say buffered/registered, some say non - registered; 
most say get ECC, some say non-ECC will work.  

I decided to try PC 100 registered ECC, and looked for CAS 
latency 2.  The best deal retail looked like Crucial, at about 
$80 per 256 meg stick.

I saw an eBay listing for 1 G (4 x 256) of Corsair PC100 ECC 
register CL 2, and bought it.  When it came i put it in right 
away - had to fiddle around a bit, but it works great if the 256 
meg pieces are in banks 0 and 1, and a couple DEC original 64 
meg pieces in bank 2.  SRM detects the full 1152 megs.  
AlphaBios indicates there are 1152 megs, but the memory test 
stops at 1024 megs.

The guy I bought it from says he has plenty more at $165 plus $5 
shipping per Gig.  I thought I'd pass it along.  You can contact 
him at  turquoise@angelfire.com 

FWIW.

jn



