On Sun, Jul 20, 2003 at 05:37:51AM -0400, Mike A. Harris wrote:
> 
> Actually, the bug is in tuxracer itself.  There is a Mesa
> environment variable that escapes my mind that disables VTXFMT 
> and/or TCL which works around the bug in tuxracer.  It's on the 
> dri-devel list archives somewhere, or you can probably just ping 
> Michel Daenzer about it.

Yup, found the reference, and setting RADEON_TCL_FORCE_DISABLE=1
will clean up the vast majority of glitches in tuxracer.

Do you know if anyone has volunteered to fix the bugs in tuxracer? :-)

> Dunno about any sproingies issue unless it is Alpha specific.  
> File a bug with details if you like, for tracking at least.

Just in the off-chance that disabling TCL might affect some of the
xscreensavers that I've noticed degradation in between 4.1.0 and
4.3.0, I've retried the problematic ones and found:

1. no TCL helps "superquadrics" regain its speed

2. no TCL appears to make no difference in slowdown of "sproingies"

3. no TCL is disastrous to "pipes", it hangs the entire machine!
  (note that under 4.1.0, rendering is weird, but stock 4.3.0 is fine)

I'll try to do some testing against the CVS tree and see if it makes
a difference...

 --Jay++

